<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajendra Singh of Jaintia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">deposed 1835</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajendra Singh was the last raja of the Jaintia kingdom in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. After subjects of the British were seized in his territory and allegedly sacrificed, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> annexed his lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sylhet">Sylhet</a> plains and then the Jaintia Hills in 1835, deposing him. The kingdom's territory was then administered as part of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>.</p></div>
